# Case: Real guest close, background capture and second launch
# Mode: native
# Environment: disposable-guest
# Purpose: Verify that closing the native main window preserves capture and second launch reopens the existing owner.
# Steps:
#   Close the focused owned main window through physical Alt+F4, offer fresh text while hidden, launch the same application identity again, then reopen history and quit at cleanup.
# Expected:
#   The hidden main window retains its service and captures exact fresh content; second launch exits and preserves the service generation; the original window becomes visible; explicit Quit reaps the owner and service.
# Forbidden:
#   Closing unrelated applications, replacing the active service, or treating a process fixture as a native close.

system-board-write 'UNIC-D lifecycle startup baseline'
start
system-key Alt+F4
system-window unic hidden
system-board-write 'UNIC-D capture while main hidden 中文'
history-count 1
system-second-launch
system-window unic visible
ui-wait listItem 'UNIC-D capture while main hidden 中文'
screenshot reopened-existing-owner
